{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Edges and their identity.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":" lists every edge once (each copy of a parallel edge, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each self-loop, once), and an edge’s position in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":" is its identity. The edge is reached"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from both its endpoints through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":", always at that one position, so a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keyed by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Edges.Index"},{"type":"text","text":" (a weight) is the same in both directions. Positions are valid until the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph is mutated."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Counting."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Neighborhoods count edge ends. A vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"w ≠ v"},{"type":"text","text":" appears in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"neighbors(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once per edge between them. A self-loop has both its ends at "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":", so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" appears in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"neighbors(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":" twice per loop, and the loop’s position twice in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(Boost’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"adjacency_list"},{"type":"text","text":", LEMON, igraph). "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"degree(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is the length of either, so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"self-loop counts 2 and the degrees sum to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"2 * edgeCount"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Vertex and edge indices.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" As for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":": with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexIndexBound"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexIndex(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" maps the vertices one-to-one onto "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexIndexBound"},{"type":"text","text":", and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"neighborIndices(ofIndex:)"},{"type":"text","text":" gives adjacency in index space. A representation with dense edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indices also reports "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeIndexBound"},{"type":"text","text":", and then "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeIndex(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" maps edge positions"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one-to-one onto "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<edgeIndexBound"},{"type":"text","text":" (Boost’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edge_index"},{"type":"text","text":", petgraph’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EdgeIndexable"},{"type":"text","text":"), so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithms that mark edges (bridges, cut vertices, Euler tours) keep that state in arrays too."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdgeIndices(ofIndex:)"},{"type":"text","text":" lists them parallel to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"neighborIndices(ofIndex:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Laws.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Every conformer satisfies:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"vertexCount == vertices.count","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the vertices are distinct, and every edge’s endpoints are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices; ","type":"text"},{"code":"edgeCount == edges.count","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For every vertex ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdges(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lists the position of each edge with an end at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" once per end (a self-loop twice); each such edge has ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as an endpoint;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"oppositeVertex(to: v, acrossEdgeAt: e)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges[e].oppositeVertex(to: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":";","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"neighbors(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the opposite vertices in the same order; ","type":"text"},{"code":"degree(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is their","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"count.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The degrees sum to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"2 * edgeCount"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains(edge:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is true exactly for the edges in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":", in either orientation, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains"},{"type":"text","text":" is false (and does not trap) for anything"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"absent."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Asking again gives the same answer.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With vertex indices, "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is in index order: "},{"code":"vertex(atIndex: i)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the "},{"code":"i","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"th vertex."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"With vertex indices, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"neighborIndices(ofIndex: vertexIndex(of: v))"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"neighbors(of: v)"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"mapped through ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexIndex(of:)"},{"text":", in the same order.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With vertex indices, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges(ofIndex: vertexIndex(of: v))"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With edge indices, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeIndexBound == edgeCount"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeIndex(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is one-to-one onto"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<edg